<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Oct bankruptcies rise 9.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Belgian Oct bankruptcies rise 9.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company bankruptcies in Belgium rose by 9.3 percent to 808 in October compared with the year ago month, Belgian trade and company data group Infotrade said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Infotrade said 2,300 jobs had been lost as a result of the bankruptcies.</p>
<p>In the first 10 months of 1996 a total of 6,118 companies went bankrupt, up 5.1 percent from 5,819 in the same 1995 period.</p>
